    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0368" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/2669: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-24T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:33
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>93. Referring to your telegram via Paris regarding European relief,<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d265-f1"/> and my 87, March 17, 4 p.m.<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d265-f2"/></p>
                <p>Swedish Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me his Government expects shortly to
                    send representatives to Copenhagen to confer with Sir William Goode<anchor
                        n="19" xml:id="d265-f3"/> whom the British Government is sending there in
                    connection with proposed meeting of neutrals in Paris for discussion of
                    financial relief in central Europe. I understand Swedish Government has also
                    communicated with Norway, Denmark, Holland and other neutrals regarding this
                    matter. British Government has wired British Minister here to inquire if Swedish
                    Government would send representative to meet Goode in Copenhagen.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d265-f1" n="17" xml:id="d265-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 518, Mar. 12, to the Ambassador in France, <ref target="#pg264"
                        >p. 264</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f2" n="18" xml:id="d265-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f3" n="19" xml:id="d265-f3-content">
                <p>British Director of Relief Missions.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
